## Qt 6.11 License

The Qt frontend uses Qt 6.11 under **LGPLv3** (Lesser General Public License v3).
The Rust core crates remain **MIT**.

### LGPLv3 Compliance Requirements

| Requirement | How to satisfy |
|-------------|---------------|
| Dynamic linking | Link Qt as `.dll`/`.so` — never statically link Qt |
| User relinkability | Ship C++ `.obj` files or Qt frontend source so users can relink against modified Qt |
| No Qt modification disclosure | Only required if Qt itself is modified |
| License notice | Include Qt LGPLv3 notice in About dialog and `docs/legal/LICENSES.md` |

### Permitted Qt Modules (LGPLv3)

`Qt Core`, `Qt Gui`, `Qt Quick`, `Qt Quick Controls 2`, `Qt SVG`, `Qt PrintSupport`, `Qt Concurrent`, `Qt Network`

### Forbidden Qt Modules (GPL-only — cannot use in this project)

`Qt Charts`, `Qt Data Visualization`, `Qt Quick 3D Studio` (some editions)

### Rust Core License

The Rust core (`libseamly_core`) is MIT-licensed. No source disclosure is required.
The FFI boundary (C ABI) provides clean separation — LGPL does not propagate across it.

## Do Not

- Modify binary assets under `assets/images/` or font files unless requested
- Remove license notices or headers
- Statically link Qt (violates LGPLv3 relinking requirement)
- Use GPL-only Qt modules (Qt Charts, Qt Data Visualization)